{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/componentmacro"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Essentials"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro"},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article","title":"Generating components with the component macro"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Implement registration, cloning, snapshots and inspection for a component from its stored properties."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The optional ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECSMacros"},{"text":" product provides the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component"},{"text":" macro.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"It turns a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"struct"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"enum"},{"text":" into a component and implements a set of component protocols from its stored properties, so you don’t have to write that code by hand:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"table","header":"row","rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Protocol","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Generated","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Enables","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/RegistrableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"stable ","type":"text"},{"code":"componentTypeName","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nexus.register(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.registeredComponentTypes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.componentType(named:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/CloneableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"init(cloning:context:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"clone(context:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"entity.clone()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.clone(entities:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.clone(into:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SerializableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"CodingKeys","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"init(from:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"encode(to:)","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"nexus.encodeSnapshot(using:handling:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.restoreSnapshot(from:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"nexus.decodeSnapshot(from:using:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Nexus: Codable","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/InspectableComponent"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"componentProperties","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"generic inspection, e.g. in editors","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/DefaultInitializable"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" if every stored property has a default value (structs)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"key path assignment, state machines","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Component"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"static let componentIndex","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"typed lookups read a plain static instead of taking the registry lock","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The core ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECS"},{"text":" library stays dependency free. Only ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECSMacros"},{"text":" depends on ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/swiftlang\/swift-syntax"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"All protocols can also be implemented by hand without the macro.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Adding the product","level":3,"anchor":"Adding-the-product"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Add the product to your target. It does not re-export ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECS"},{"text":": add the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FirebladeECS"},{"text":" product too and import both modules in every file that uses ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":[".target(","    name: \"YourTargetName\",","    dependencies: [","        .product(name: \"FirebladeECS\", package: \"ecs\"),","        .product(name: \"FirebladeECSMacros\", package: \"ecs\")","    ])"]},{"type":"heading","text":"Declaring components","level":3,"anchor":"Declaring-components"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import FirebladeECS","import FirebladeECSMacros","","@Component","struct Transform {","    var position: SIMD3<Float> = .zero","    var parent: EntityIdentifier?","    @ComponentIgnored var cachedMatrix: [Float] = []  \/\/ still cloned, but not serialized or inspected","}","","@Component(excluding: .serializable)  \/\/ runtime-only component","struct RenderHandle: @unchecked Sendable {","    var handle: Int = 0","}"]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The stable type name defaults to the fully qualified type name. Declare "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static let componentTypeName"},{"type":"text","text":" to override it."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After renaming a persisted type, list its former names in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"static let componentTypeNameAliases"},{"type":"text","text":" so existing snapshots keep loading. See "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component(excluding:)"},{"type":"text","text":" takes a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ComponentMacroFeatures"},{"type":"text","text":" set: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".cloneable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".serializable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".inspectable"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".defaultInit"},{"type":"text","text":". Registration is always implemented."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@ComponentIgnored"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps a stored property out of serialization and inspection. Ignored properties are still cloned and need a default value."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Serialized properties need an explicit type annotation. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"let"},{"type":"text","text":" constants with an initial value are not serialized."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Members you declare yourself are not generated. Declaring any of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CodingKeys"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init(from:)"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"encode(to:)"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves serialization entirely to you."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The generated initializers live in an extension, so a struct keeps its memberwise initializer. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"public"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"package"},{"type":"text","text":" struct, and a struct that declares initializers, gets a generated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"type":"text","text":" in its body (the implicit "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"init()"},{"text":" is internal and disappears next to declared initializers); an internal struct without initializers keeps the implicit one.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"An enum is cloned as a whole and listed without properties. It is serialized only if it declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" itself, and it gets ","type":"text"},{"code":"DefaultInitializable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" only if it declares ","type":"text"},{"code":"init()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The macro stores "},{"code":"static let componentIndex = registeredComponentIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The index still comes from the registry at first access, so it cannot collide with a lazily assigned one. Declare your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"componentIndex","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to opt out.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Value types and diagnostics","level":3,"anchor":"Value-types-and-diagnostics"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Component"},{"text":" reports an error when it is applied to a class: components are value types, so use a struct or enum. The nexus also asserts once per component type, in debug builds, that a hand-written conformance is not a class.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A stored property spelled ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity?","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[Entity]"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"code":"Set<Entity>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"[Key: Entity]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is an error with a fix-it that replaces ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" by ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityIdentifier"},{"text":". An ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity"},{"text":" keeps its nexus alive and is not valid after a copy, a clone or a snapshot, while an identifier is a plain value that the clone context remaps. The macro sees syntax only: an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Entity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" behind a typealias or in a nested type is not diagnosed and stays a convention.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Registering, cloning and snapshots","anchor":"Registering-cloning-and-snapshots","level":3,"type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let nexus = Nexus()","try nexus.register([Transform.self, RenderHandle.self])","","\/\/ Clone a whole world; entity references (`parent`) are remapped to the clones.","let playMode = Nexus()","try nexus.clone(into: playMode)","","\/\/ Export and import all serializable components, keyed by their stable type names.","var encoder = JSONEncoder()","let data = try nexus.encodeSnapshot(using: &encoder, handling: .skip)","var decoder = JSONDecoder()","try playMode.decodeSnapshot(from: data, using: &decoder)"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Component types are registered automatically the first time an instance is assigned."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Register them explicitly before decoding snapshots that reference them."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusSnapshot","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" starts with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"formatVersion"},{"text":" and keeps the original entity identifiers.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Decoding creates new entities, remaps entity references to them through an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/EntityReferenceResolver"},{"text":", and rejects snapshots written in a newer format version.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Benchmarks":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"See how FirebladeECS revisions compare on a shared workload suite, and run the comparison yourself."}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/benchmarks","kind":"article","title":"Benchmarks","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Benchmarks"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/MigratingToFirebladeECS2":{"kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a project from FirebladeECS 1.x to 2.0: components become value types, and every write goes through the nexus."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","type":"topic","title":"Migrating to FirebladeECS 2","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/migratingtofirebladeecs2"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","abstract":[{"text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values.","type":"text"}],"role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents","kind":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","type":"topic"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEvent":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A marker protocol for all Nexus events."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexusevent","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEvent","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"NexusEvent","fragments":[{"text":